/**
 * Where the five from Mars take the motion v. 15 sorts their sight by (C430). The Sun, the Moon and the nodes have theirs from v. 19 under every one.
 *
 * `SKY`: The sky's: each graha's speed in the transit chart against its mean daily motion ([`Motion::by_speed`]), the mean the *Surya Siddhanta*'s revolutions give (I.29 to 34), Mercury's and Venus's the Sun's. The tika gives vv. 16–18 as the motion "without computing the grahas", so the computed motion is the one they stand in for.
 * `SUN`: vv. 16–18's, read off the Sun's sign counted from the graha's ([`Motion::by_the_sun`]). A graha in the Sun's own sign is unseen (v. 18) and the verses give it no motion, so it takes the sky's. The rule makes Mercury and Venus never retrograde (§8.2).
 * `GIVEN`: The caller's, for Mars, Mercury, Jupiter, Venus and Saturn in that order, at every instant asked.
 */
export type SarvatobhadraMotion =
  | 'SKY'
  | 'SUN'
